# The changelog is append-at-the-top, so two branches that each ship an entry
# insert at the same line and collide — every time, whatever the content.
# union keeps BOTH insertions instead of raising a conflict; the repo's stamp
# tool then assigns the version numbers (authors write `v: null`).
# See polecat-platform docs/SHELL-API.md § the fleet changelog contract.
#
# Hazard, accepted knowingly: two branches editing the SAME EXISTING entry
# differently would keep both copies rather than conflict. The contract check
# catches that — versions must be strictly decreasing — and editing a shipped
# entry is rare, while prepending happens every run.
js/changelog.js merge=union
